// PIN FMT-006 — an output statement is never wrapped.
//
// `>>` and `>>~` are terminated by the end of the line, so breaking a long call
// across lines inside one does not reformat the statement: it ENDS it, and
// leaves the rest as a fragment that does not parse. The gate refused the file,
// correctly, and `Chaturanga/दर्शनम्/चित्रणम्.zy` — which draws a board this way —
// could not be formatted at all.
//
// Line length is a preference. Emitting a program that does not parse is not a
// trade-off against it.
//
// What has to be long is the ARGUMENT LIST, not the line: the wrap decision
// measures the arguments. The first draft had a 116-character line whose call
// was short, so nothing wrapped and the pin held while the guard was reverted.
// Verified by reverting.
centrado(t, w, r) { <~ t }

recortado(t, w, r) { <~ t }

fila_actual = 1
columna_inicial = 1
titulo_del_tablero_completo = "tablero"
ancho_interior_disponible = 20
relleno_por_defecto = " "

>>~ (fila_actual, columna_inicial) > "│" centrado(recortado(titulo_del_tablero_completo, ancho_interior_disponible, relleno_por_defecto), ancho_interior_disponible, relleno_por_defecto) "│"
